{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A hard cutover to a new design-system major version breaks every consuming app at once; a shim that keeps the old API working, paired with a codemod, lets each team migrate on its own schedule.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Ship the new implementation with a compatibility shim active by default so a semver-correct major bump doesn't become a synchronized outage, and pair it with an automated codemod so migrating isn't manual per-app work.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Instrument the shim itself so "is it safe to remove" is a real usage number, not a calendar guess, and check for dual-package hazards when some consumers migrate slower than others.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
